From d1cc167bc296c1d5666462232658e4b8d0925e93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:28:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary, language: where Dolby Vision made from HDR10+ takes
 its level 1, and that adapting follows HDR10+

The row "RPU" of the Dolby Vision page said "made from the HDR10+ metadata".
It now says what is made of them: level 1 from the HDR10+ statistics, without
the tone curve, which Dolby Vision has no place for. The help of "HDR10 and
HDR10+ adapted to the display" says that an HDR10+ video is adapted scene by
scene from its own data, and by the studio's tone curve where it carries one.
---
 addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po    |  2 +-
 .../language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po        |  6 +++---
 .../language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po        | 10 +++++-----
 .../language/resource.language.es_es/strings.po        | 10 +++++-----
 .../language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po        | 10 +++++-----
 5 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
