--- a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
+++ b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
@@ -27097,7 +27097,7 @@ msgstr ""
 #. Hades: help of setting "videoscreen.hadeshdr10adapt"; translated in Estuary (#32281)
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 msgctxt "#40985"
-msgid "Lets Hades adapt HDR10 and HDR10+ pictures to your display's peak brightness itself, instead of leaving it to the display. Useful for projectors and TVs that do this poorly; it uses graphics power. Never (the default): the picture goes out as mastered and the display adapts it. Always: every HDR10 or HDR10+ video that states its peak. Automatic: only videos brighter than your display, decided once per video. The peak of your display is the one set for Dolby Vision as HDR10 where that is on, else the one in its EDID. kodi.log gives the cost every 10 seconds. Takes effect from the next video."
+msgid "Lets Hades adapt HDR10 and HDR10+ pictures to your display's peak brightness itself, instead of leaving it to the display. Useful for projectors and TVs that do this poorly; it uses graphics power. An HDR10+ video is adapted scene by scene from its own data, and by the studio's tone curve where it carries one. Never (the default): the picture goes out as mastered and the display adapts it. Always: every HDR10 or HDR10+ video that states its peak. Automatic: only videos brighter than your display, decided once per video. The peak of your display is the one set for Dolby Vision as HDR10 where that is on, else the one in its EDID. kodi.log gives the cost every 10 seconds. Takes effect from the next video."
 msgstr ""
 
 #. Hades: value of setting "videoscreen.hadesdvcm40": added where the video has neither a v4.0 part nor trims (level 2), decided once per video; translated in Estuary (#32274)
